SUMMARY:Epic #5 - The Lavielle Loop
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/epic-5)**\n\n***Welcome to
  The Epics!***\n\n***Through this series\, we will embark together on five
  of the most legendary and challenging adventures anywhere in Ontario.***\
 n\n**History**\nDeep in the interior of Algonquin Park lies a chain of lak
 es that remains a bucket list trip for serious paddlers. The Lavieille Loo
 p is a high-endurance expedition named after one of the most beautiful lak
 es in a park full of incredible scenery.\n\nThis is a route of extremes: f
 rom the crystal-clear expanse of **Lake Lavieille** to the winding\, moose
 -heavy waters of the **Crow River**\, culminating in the legendary 5.5km *
 *Dickson-Bonfield portage**\, this is a true test of grit.\n\nThis expedit
 ion is inspired by the Meanest Link\, a legendary challenge created by our
  friends and partners at Algonquin Outfitters.\n\nDesigned by Alex Hurley 
 and Gord Baker as a tribute to AO’s founder\, Bill Swift Sr.\, the Link 
 was built to push the limits of exploration and self-reliance. While our l
 oop covers a specific\, scenic section of this historic network\, we’ve 
 designed this Epic to channel that same spirit of adventure and respect fo
 r the park’s heritage.\n\nLearn more about the history and the original 
 route of the Meanest Link on the [Algonquin Outfitters website](https://al
 gonquinoutfitters.com/about/meanest-link-history/).\n‍\n**What You Need 
 to Know**\nThis journey is a true ode to Algonquin Park. We’ve carved ou
 t a nearly 100km route\, taking us from the massive waters of Lake Opeongo
 \, along the winding Crow River\, and into the remote reaches of Lake Lavi
 eille before heading back down to Opeongo. By doing this in early Septembe
 r\, we catch the park at its absolute best: the bugs are gone\, the weathe
 r is beautiful\, and the wildlife is active along the riverbanks.\n\nAwait
 ing us in the second half of our journey is the notorious Dickson-Bonfield
  portage. At over 5km\,this is the longest single portage in Algonquin Par
 k. It’s relatively flat but a huge challenge and\, once you set your can
 oe down at Bonfield Lake\, you’ll have earned your place among the most 
 dedicated paddlers in the province.\n\nThis trip requires a high level of 
 fitness and a genuine willingness to embrace the challenge of a 5km trek w
 ith a canoe on your shoulders. For those willing to take on the challenge\
 , this offers the most rewarding sense of accomplishment you can find on t
 he water.\n\n**What's Included:**\n\n* *2 expert guides with advanced wild
 erness skills and medical training*\n* *Rentals for lightweight canoes\, P
 FDs and paddles*\n* *All camp meals\, cooking equipment and mess kits*\n* 
 *All safety equipment (including first aid kits and water purification)*\n
 * *Tents and all the camping equipment you'll need (sleeping bags and pads
  are available for rent)*\n* *All permits and campsite bookings for the wh
 ole trip*\n* *A preparatory information session*\n* *Detailed trip plan wi
 th packing lists\, maps and the indigenous history of the route we're foll
 owing*\n* *Extensive planning to ensure your safety throughout the adventu
 re*\n* *A custom\, iron-on patch to immortalize your unforgettable adventu
 re*\n\n***Epics are mentally and physically demanding adventures\, and par
 ticipation isn’t automatically guaranteed. These expeditions require ski
 ll\, determination and teamwork to get through.***\n\n***To help ensure a 
 safe and rewarding experience for all\, anyone who has not previously comp
 leted an Epic will need to fill out a short questionnaire so we can assess
  readiness together.***\n\n***Your level of fitness and outdoors experienc
 e will play a role in this process. Having certain adventures under your b
 elt will ensure you have the right skills and preparation for these kinds 
 of experiences. These include:***\n\n* ***Any Wilder Series adventure\, in
 cluding the upcoming Wilder Loop***\n* ***Any Survivalist Series adventure
 \, including Introduction to Navigation or Cold Exposure***\n* ***Canoe Fo
 undations Clinic***\n* ***Hilton Falls Mega***\n* ***Any other adventure w
 ith 4 or 5 star difficulty***\n\n***If you register for an Epic and are no
 t approved\, you will receive a refund in full.***\n\n**Highlights**\n**An
  Epic Challenge -** Our longest and most ambitious epic will be the ultima
 te reward.\n**Dickson-Bonfield Portage -** The legendary portage spans 5.4
 km and is the longest single carry in the park.\n‍**Secret Lake Sanctuar
 ies** \\- True crown jewels of the Algonquin interior\\\, there are no eas
 y routes to the lakes we will be seeing\\\, which keep them incredibly qui
 et and pristine\\.\n\n**Event cost: $1185+HST. $50 optional transport also
  available. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/advent
 ures/epic-5)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is delibera
 te about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-chan
 ging magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers rang
 e from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to 
 Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don
 't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community
  members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but 
 small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [
 www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
